ty","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1a1e1c6efd30e05cc7c61aa9eb5103998e0eec21.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1a1e1c6efd30e05cc7c61aa9eb5103998e0eec21.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 13 at 8:25PM MDT until August 13 at 11:30PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Central Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1130 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 825 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges\nindicated heavy rain due to thunderstorms. This may cause urban\nand small stream flooding. Between 0.5 and 2 inches of rain have\nfallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nAntelope Creek, Wildcat Creek, Bijou Creek, East Prong Wildcat\nCreek, Rock Creek, South Platte River and Badger Creek.\nAdditional rainfall amounts up to 1.5 inches are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nFort Morgan, Log Lane Village, Adena School and Fort Morgan\nAirport.","ends":"2026-08-13T23:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.49788c32fbb6d4af44ef4189dd0d1bbdf14093a1.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.49788c32fbb6d4af44ef4189dd0d1bbdf14093a1.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-14T02:13:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 140213 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 813 PM MDT Thu Aug 13 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash Flooding possible on Aspen Acres Burn scar through this evening. - Monsoon moisture stays over us through the weekend with locally heavy rainfall and flash flooding possible, especially for flood prone areas like burn